mantle rm462
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_wystan_coalmarsh
title the low-sling roofline
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk judges_a_future_windows_height_by_the_rooftop_birds
likes plum_tart roof_birds market_bustle frosty_mornings
dislikes night_noise stale_bread
fears putting_down_the_hope_of_a_higher_room
hopes a_window_level_with_the_roof_birds
topics work +0.5 animals +0.4 faith +0.4 prices +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures the height of a future window against the feet of roof birds and saves the longest complaints for the walk with no one listening.
words
oath! = Jam my right sheave | Shorten my honest lift
saying! = Lift level and look up | A bird owes no roof rent
slingline = a broad lifting strap | a well-laid sling
rooftrace = a jagged line of slate | a line of sunlit ridges
bootrail = a raised threshold | a short firm step
purseend = my uphill penny | a little window money
tartmark = a purple crust end | a piece of dark plum pastry
frostiron = a white lip on iron | a line of crystals
crowdbit = an open elbow's width | a narrow eddy in the crowd
breadchip = a floury heel | a bit of hard crust
birdheel = a pair of quick dark feet | two little claws
payline = a square pay mark | a sum with an honest edge
liftcloth = a folded shoulder rag | a soft strap pad

grown

opinion houses against 1 : A better connection can take a post. It cannot hoist the load still standing where the work was left.
opinion road mixed 1 : A hill is lovely to look up at until you have to carry somebody else's expensive parcel all the way.
opinion watch mixed 1 : I'd like as much protection for a working back as for the bale that's riding on it.
opinion city mixed 1 : From a higher window I'd see another part of the city without first leaving home.
opinion church for 2 : A second willing pair of hands deserves thanks before the first one lets the weight go.
opinion festivals for 1 : I enjoy the market pushing and talking while there's still room for a carrier to set a load down safe.
line greet : Step into view alongside my end of the work.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. Give the road behind you a little clearance.
line greet.return : I can hear you above the market, distinctly enough.
line farewell : May your next climb be more for yourself than for a parcel.
line farewell.return : Carry your sights high and set your feet where they belong.
line ask.how : How heavily has the day been leaning on your better shoulder?
line answer.how : Good for the work if I take my knee's advice on the turn.
line react.news : I'll hear what that weighed when the cargo first set out.
line react.news.known : Heard that one passing the first row of roofs.
line react.news.new : A fresh shape above the old roofline, then.
line react.news.doubt : That sounds weightier than the hands behind it can account for.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : A small celebration somewhere with a view would fit that news.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd set the load down and be there to take part of the strain.
line decline : I won't complain to the whole market just because one account is crooked.
line accept_decline : Your choice. The sling needn't go on every shoulder.
line thank : You waited till both my feet had a grip before letting go.
line deflect_thanks : There was work needing a willing end of a strap.
line reassure : A climb doesn't lose its purpose because a knee calls one pause.
line sympathise : Stand clear here a minute. I'll keep the traffic moving round us.
line ack : I know which end you're carrying now.
line preclose : I'd best move before a new heap grows round my soles.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My working stretch round #self.workplace# can look very different depending on which end of a sling you hold.
b : Which end's harder? | Who's in charge of the pace?
a : The one with less room for a boot. I'll swap gladly if a second pair of hands is getting pinned against a post. | The slowest sound footing. Shouting doesn't put a plank under anybody's heel.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take two risers when the knee agrees and one when the load claims the casting vote.
b : Who's chairman of that arrangement? | Do you enjoy the climb?
a : The board beneath my sole. It can take us all out of office in one short slide. | Going uphill towards my own hopes, yes. An errand for another purse takes rather longer to look romantic.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like the line the little roof birds make with their feet.
b : Why feet and not wings? | Can you see them that far up?
a : Wings can get anywhere. Feet tell me which precise part of the town is worth coming down for. | Two black pricks on a bright ridge are often enough. It's the height from my own feet that interests me.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save the corner where the plum has got past the crust and scorched a little.
b : Why save the burnt bit? | Wouldn't a fresh plum be cheaper?
a : To my mouth that's the part with its own clean edge and a little smoke round the sweet. | A plum will do nicely. Sometimes I can afford somebody else's time folding the pastry.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a window with room to see a roof bird during the last evening prayer.
b : What would that add? | Is your present room too low for prayer?
a : A reminder to come down to my own task when the prayer's done, as a bird eventually comes off a roof. | I'd be in a very poor way if a flight of stairs could put the Bright One out of hearing.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the height of the room I want in courses of brick, not in fine names.
b : How many courses? | Would you leave the low streets altogether?
a : Enough to see over the wall opposite. Some wants get surprisingly ordinary once they're measured. | I'd go back readily when I chose. I'd like the choice to belong to whoever lives in the room.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a frosty morning the highest roof catches a little line of white first.
b : What does the nip tell you? | Do you care for the cold?
a : Where the sun will reach me if the work takes me over to the open side of the street. | In the face, yes. Under a loaded boot I would prefer the stone thawed and plain.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A busy market can make me feel easier even on a day without coin to spend.
b : Like being jostled? | What catches your eye in a market?
a : I prefer to see a lot of different purposes in motion. I'll do without a basket shoved into my back. | A stallholder able to hand over one little parcel without keeping the next caller waiting for a great show.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This knee sometimes reads approaching weather more faithfully than it reads my instructions.
b : Will you let it set your pace? | Do you always feel it before rain?
a : I have a lot more use for a whole knee tomorrow than for the boast of one extra load today. | No. I'd make an untrustworthy instrument for telling anybody when to bring the washing in.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dislike an offer of pity while my hands are full of something I chose to carry.
b : What help would you take? | Is pride making it harder?
a : A gate held open without anybody announcing the decline of my limbs to the whole street. | A bit. I try to recognise that before the next perfectly civil offer comes along.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : No public complaint of mine will recover the place I lost to somebody better connected.
b : Then why keep quiet? | Would you give the place another chance?
a : I want whoever hears my case to be in a position to do something. The rest of the street is busy with its own loads. | For fair terms. Not because I'm prepared to swallow the old unfairness and call it seasonal weather.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can keep a penny for a high window without thinking every warm meal is stealing the view.
b : Where do you draw the line? | Do you tell anyone what you're saving?
a : At going hungry. I want a living body at that nice window when the rent finally comes within reach. | Enough to make the saving real, no further. A good subscription of comments won't cover the rent.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember looking down from the top of a loaded cart and seeing a roof bird at eye height.
b : What did you see in its face? | Didn't you feel unsteady?
a : No concern whatever about the social distinction it had just erased. A very sensible bird. | I was standing still and holding the rail. My dream includes a floor with a smaller taste for rocking.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hard week turns a good loaf stale while I'm stretching it towards the next.
b : What happens to the heel? | Would you abandon the climb for now?
a : It goes below a ladle of stew. Once soaked it's fit for a tired set of teeth again. | I might set less by. A penny counted towards a window hasn't committed me to starving underneath it.

scene home_2
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noise is less tolerable to a back due early to the load.
b : Do you ask kindly for quiet? | What if the sound's just a loose board?
a : Once. If it needs another asking, I'd still like somebody to warn me once my own voice is getting too large. | Give me daylight and a spare nail. A plank has fewer excuses available than a wakeful crowd.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could sit at a market's edge identifying which roofs the birds have deserted for crumbs.
b : Wouldn't you miss the bargaining? | Are the birds shameless?
a : I'd hear quite enough of it free of charge. The birds give me a better view for the same seat. | They're doing their own loading. I feel some professional sympathy for a bird carrying a very large crust.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd point out a clear space for a newcomer when the crowd closes up behind a moving load.
b : Where's the safe place? | Would you ask for the hand's name?
a : Off to one side, heels against a post until the swinging part has passed. A look is worth more than guessing. | After the load's down. A good name won't stop a foot being caught.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account being carried is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Was it a heavy load of evidence? | Would you go to claim it as true?
a : Words only. I've seen an empty crate get the respect due a full one on account of a strenuous-looking carrier. | Not till there's something more substantial to put my shoulder under.

story bird [topic=animals]
  : A bird planted one claw on a roof tile and the other on a hanging rope and thought it was measuring a great building.
  : The rope shifted, the foot lifted and my learned surveyor discovered a piece of crust on the tile.
  b : Did the survey end?
  : It had reached the only figure that interested a hungry bird. I rather approved of the result.

story tart [topic=food]
  : I laid a tart on a level board and set my shoulder against the load that stood underneath.
  : When the board rose one end of the pastry made a bold little departure.
  b : Did you catch it?
  : With the clean inside of my wrist. I got my dinner and a purple stripe where no stripe had previously been needed.

story tread [topic=memories]
  : I tried a shallow stair with the high striding pace of a much steeper climb. My last step went entirely into air.
  : I tried to give the unspent step a dignified conclusion.
  b : Did anyone believe it was intentional?
  : One small admirer applauded gallantly. I hope I never have to repeat the performance for a paid audience.

rule @shore
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room on the firm board for the trailing heel. | Look past the shoulders for the empty bit of route.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Listen to the foot at the far end before lifting. | The load won't tell us which carrier needs another breath.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say White line up high and a new bit of day coming. | A high view makes the low work feel like a beginning.

rule @tart
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the plum streak clear of the lifting strap. | Crisp edge first if it's going up a steep road.
dlg resident.hub : Stand where the load won't come round on you while we talk.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : I work around #self.workplace#. No sling's properly balanced till the feet at both ends can move.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This made it past the crowded part of the day. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Market talk has #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm repeating words. Ask elsewhere for a witness prepared to carry that account into court.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I recognised you above the market before you got near the sling.
dlg resident.bye : Good footing for the climb and a clear look from the top.

graft resident.hub
choice Would one high window make that much difference? -> roof_window
node roof_window
say At present I see the undersides of birds. I wish to open my eyes on a bird standing still with the roof level beneath us both.
choice Would anything else have to change? -> roof_settle
choice I'll look up when I pass. -> hub
node roof_settle
say Only what it takes to pay for the room and come through its door with enough light left to notice. I'm working at both ends.
choice I'll look up when I pass. -> hub
